From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:08:21 +0200
Subject: blit: a faster scalar 8888 alpha blit between different formats

Without SIMD (PowerPC: no SSE4.1, AVX2, LSX or NEON path) every 32-bit
sprite with per-pixel alpha blitted onto a surface of another 8888 format
goes through Blit8888to8888PixelAlphaSwizzle. Its macro read the four
shifts and the alpha mask from both formats for every pixel (the stores
through dst keep the compiler from holding them in registers), and blended
fully transparent and fully opaque pixels like any other. On the PS3 that
loop was 55% of Warmux's frame (SDL 1.2 through sdl12-compat: ARGB8888
sprites onto the XRGB8888 screen).

Now the shifts are locals, the RGB bytes are moved only when their places
differ (ARGB8888 onto XRGB8888 keeps them: one mask), and a pixel with
alpha 0 leaves dst alone, one with alpha 255 stores the source, exactly
what the blend gives at those values. The results are bit-identical to
before (a host test compares the two loops on 11 million random pixels,
every 8888 layout pair, both FACTOR_BLEND_8888 variants).

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/video/SDL_blit_A.c b/src/video/SDL_blit_A.c
--- a/src/video/SDL_blit_A.c
+++ b/src/video/SDL_blit_A.c
@@ -1071,17 +1071,49 @@ static void Blit8888to8888PixelAlphaSwizzle(SDL_BlitInfo *info)
 
     SDL_Get8888AlphaMaskAndShift(dstfmt, &dstAmask, &dstAshift);
 
+    /* Walnut: the shifts in locals (the macro read them from the formats for every pixel: the
+       compiler can't keep them in registers across the stores through dst), the RGB bytes moved
+       only when their places differ (ARGB8888 onto XRGB8888 keeps them), and a pixel's alpha of 0
+       or 255 decided without the blend (the blend gives exactly dst or src there). Without SIMD
+       (PowerPC) this is the path for every 32-bit sprite blitted onto a window surface of another
+       format: 55% of Warmux's frame on the PS3. */
+    const Uint32 sA = srcfmt->Ashift, sR = srcfmt->Rshift, sG = srcfmt->Gshift, sB = srcfmt->Bshift;
+    const Uint32 dR = dstfmt->Rshift, dG = dstfmt->Gshift, dB = dstfmt->Bshift;
+    const Uint32 dAmask = dstfmt->Amask;
+    const bool same_rgb = (sR == dR && sG == dG && sB == dB);
+    const Uint32 rgbmask = (0xFFu << sR) | (0xFFu << sG) | (0xFFu << sB);
+
     while (height--) {
         int i = 0;
 
         for (; i < width; ++i) {
-            Uint32 src32 = *(Uint32 *)src;
-            Uint32 dst32 = *(Uint32 *)dst;
-            ALPHA_BLEND_SWIZZLE_8888(src32, dst32, srcfmt, dstfmt);
-            if (fill_alpha) {
-                dst32 |= dstAmask;
+            const Uint32 src32 = *(Uint32 *)src;
+            const Uint32 srcA = (src32 >> sA) & 0xFF;
+            if (srcA == 0) {
+                if (fill_alpha) {
+                    *(Uint32 *)dst |= dstAmask;
+                }
+            } else {
+                Uint32 tmp;
+                if (same_rgb) {
+                    tmp = (src32 & rgbmask) | dAmask;
+                } else {
+                    tmp = (((src32 >> sR) & 0xFF) << dR) |
+                          (((src32 >> sG) & 0xFF) << dG) |
+                          (((src32 >> sB) & 0xFF) << dB) | dAmask;
+                }
+                Uint32 dst32;
+                if (srcA == 0xFF) {
+                    dst32 = tmp;
+                } else {
+                    dst32 = *(Uint32 *)dst;
+                    FACTOR_BLEND_8888(tmp, dst32, srcA);
+                }
+                if (fill_alpha) {
+                    dst32 |= dstAmask;
+                }
+                *(Uint32 *)dst = dst32;
             }
-            *(Uint32 *)dst = dst32;
             src += 4;
             dst += 4;
         }
